01. Project Contract
SpectraCraft MUST implement this specification within the existing native Rust desktop application and preserve working engine, playback, editing, and export behavior.
The repository MUST retain this specification as SPECTRACRAFT_SPEC.md and reference the specification from project instructions used for future changes.
Product-owned crate names, binaries, modules, documentation, window titles, commands, and interface labels MUST consistently identify SpectraCraft.
SpectraCraft-owned application code, audio processing, analysis, synthesis, acoustic calculations, plotting, CLI tools, fixtures, and verification tools MUST remain Rust.
The application MUST remain a native desktop workstation.
Python, Python wrappers, browser substitutes, and promotional dashboards MUST NOT become application, engine, or verification dependencies.
Implementation MUST begin with a runnable workflow covering import, shape extraction, dry regeneration, original/dry comparison, and basic region tools.
Optional capture and plugin stages MUST build on that functioning workflow.
02. Non-Negotiable Invariants
Single-source invariant
•	One work unit contains one imported instrument performance, voice, or stem.
•	Supported chords, repeated attacks, simultaneous partials, and overlapping ringing remain valid within one source.
•	Additional performances require separate work units.
Performance-reference invariant
•	The extracted performance shape remains the immutable evidence reference.
•	Explicit correction requests operate on derived rendering instructions.
•	Source models, catalog ranges, and profile matches MUST NOT replace evidence.
Fresh-signal invariant
•	Regenerated audio consists exclusively of newly synthesized samples.
•	Original PCM, source phase, sampled attacks, copied residual audio, and original waveform fragments MUST NOT enter any processing-stage output.
•	Original playback and comparison remain isolated monitoring operations.
Dry-first invariant
•	Every processed output depends on an available regenerated dry take.
•	Microphone, room, material, and plugin settings MUST NOT participate in foundational dry synthesis.
Surgical-edit invariant
•	Every localized correction targets the regenerated dry take before capture.
•	Original audio and downstream captured audio are never surgical-edit targets.
Independent-bypass invariant
•	Every stage has an explicit bypass contract.
•	Bypass preserves settings and never substitutes original audio.
Display-isolation invariant
•	Display commands MUST NOT alter audio, performance evidence, effective DSP settings, playback position, or audio-render fingerprints.
Uncertainty invariant
•	Unsupported or ambiguous evidence remains explicitly unresolved.
•	Numerical scores, source expectations, and plausible synthesis MUST NOT convert uncertainty into claims about musical events.
State invariant
•	Every render uses explicit inputs, parameter snapshots, and dependency revisions.
•	No stage may retrieve hidden audio inputs or inherit undocumented DSP state.
Scope
•	SpectraCraft reconstructs a performance for subsequent audio work.
•	Full-mix separation, universal transcription, historical gear identification, forensic recovery, and DAW replacement are outside this contract.
