cargo fmt --all --check
cargo clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
cargo test --locked --all-targets --all-features
cargo build --locked --release --all-targets --all-features
cargo audit
cargo outdated
cargo tree -d
cargo deny check
Audit reporting
•	Identify concrete findings by severity, location, and evidence.
•	Separate confirmed bugs, potential issues, dependency advisories, and static-analysis findings.
•	Record exact commands and actual results.
•	Mark unavailable or unexecuted checks NOT RUN.
Platform claims
•	Verify each claimed platform independently through build, import, playback, state persistence, and export checks.
•	A build on one platform cannot establish another platform's runtime support.
17. Implementation Completion and Handoff
Core milestone
•	Demonstrate import of one source, saved shape/cues, source-free dry synthesis, aligned original/dry display, basic region selection, and real playback.
Surgical milestone
•	Demonstrate localized candidate generation, bounded acceptance, live region preview, independent undo/redo, and export of the current edited dry take.
Capture milestone
•	Demonstrate independent microphone and room enablement, physical scene consistency, explicit propagation accounting, and preserved dry caches.
Plugin milestone
•	Demonstrate an empty identity slot, compatible explicit processing, reset behavior, and isolation from all upstream data.
Handoff
•	Provide updated Rust source, manifests, lockfile, tests, catalog provenance, reproduction commands, and a concise changelog.
•	Separate PASS, FAIL, and NOT RUN evidence.
•	Tie every reported metric, plot, and output to actual input, cue, settings, and render identities.
•	Report remaining uncertainty and unverified listening or platform behavior.
•	Treat screenshots and numerical scores as supporting evidence rather than proof of completed audio fidelity.
